{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"plastery-nonblack-centipede","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe tests/scripts cohort contains audited comments or docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The audit is pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/scripts/test_check_config_reads_red_proof.py:1-18, 54-56, 91-93, 124-128` — Preserve live-versus-prefixed differential and unique-name control. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/scripts/test_check_config_reads.py:1-21, 145-155` — Preserve owner-resolved reads, marker semantics, and name-collision regression. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/scripts/test_check_import_walk.py:1-14, 67-73` — Preserve fresh-process isolation and scripts/provider import coverage. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/scripts/test_check_orphaned_load.py:1-22, 186-188` — Preserve read-only guarantee, PID-1/high-CPU detection, and system-daemon exclusion. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/scripts/test_cli_seam_clean_heldout.py:1-20` — Preserve observable zero-exception seam-clean contract. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/scripts/test_dependency_audit.py:1-24, 319-332, 442-454` — Preserve lane routing, logical retry schedule, and real-parser validation. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/scripts/test_llm_seam_clean_heldout.py:1-23` — Preserve seam-clean and live-per-call behavior. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/scripts/test_mcp_client_pats.py:1-27` — Preserve per-client PAT separation, SSM materialization, fail-closed behavior, and non-disclosure. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/scripts/test_mcp_server_seam_clean_heldout.py:1-14, 18-21` — Preserve zero below-seam reads and provider-boundary exceptions. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/scripts/test_mutation_sandbox.py:1-10, 91-103, 179-187, 340-347, 659-663, 724-731, 783-788` — Preserve destructive-test containment, positive child-liveness proof, capability-over-presence probes, hardened child environment, and whole-module call-site binding. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/scripts/test_normalize_ci_conclusion.py:1-24` — Preserve two-input normalization and closed output domain. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/scripts/test_observability_coldstart_e2a6.py:1-16` — Preserve cold-start seed-with-zero behavior and publish-before-persist. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/scripts/test_observability_data_disk_debris.py:1-18` — Preserve non-site debris census, real `du`, bounded dimension, and no fabricated zero on unobservable volume. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/scripts/test_observability_disk_pressure.py:1-11, 184-189, 276-280` — Preserve anchored marker counting, ineffective-reclaim persistence metric, and separate scratch-volume mount signal. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/scripts/test_observability_exit.py:1-16` — Preserve aggregate probe’s exit-zero contract while individual failures remain observable. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/scripts/test_observability_marker_anchor_8c2f.py:1-14, 199-205` — Preserve record-start anchoring and lost-history clamp behavior. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/scripts/test_observability_mcp_health_9ea3.py:1-22, 160-166, 206-218` — Preserve 401-as-healthy semantics, explicit bad-path zero, and gate-independent serving-path probe. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/scripts/test_observability_mcp_markers.py:1-18` — Preserve distinct retire-cap and memory-abort counters. Consumer: none found.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every listed location contains only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints after remediation; verified by reviewing the final diff against every Scope row.\n- [ ] Every preserve item and consumer contract in Scope remains explicit and accurate; verified by a row-by-row completion comment and the commands under Verification.\n- [ ] No executable behavior or test assertion changes; verified by the commands under Verification exiting 0.\n\n## Verification\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/scripts/test_check_config_reads_red_proof.py tests/scripts/test_check_config_reads.py tests/scripts/test_check_import_walk.py tests/scripts/test_check_orphaned_load.py tests/scripts/test_cli_seam_clean_heldout.py tests/scripts/test_dependency_audit.py tests/scripts/test_llm_seam_clean_heldout.py tests/scripts/test_mcp_client_pats.py tests/scripts/test_mcp_server_seam_clean_heldout.py tests/scripts/test_mutation_sandbox.py tests/scripts/test_normalize_ci_conclusion.py tests/scripts/test_observability_coldstart_e2a6.py tests/scripts/test_observability_data_disk_debris.py tests/scripts/test_observability_disk_pressure.py tests/scripts/test_observability_exit.py tests/scripts/test_observability_marker_anchor_8c2f.py tests/scripts/test_observability_mcp_health_9ea3.py tests/scripts/test_observability_mcp_markers.py`\n\nThe row-by-row diff review is authoritative for prose quality; the hygiene guard detects only its narrow deterministic history-token rule.","id":"ae2a-f0ec-4aad-476b","parent_id":"2d43-3c39-307e-4450","priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"tags":["comments","documentation","maintainability","grouped-remediation"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Condense comments in tests/scripts — cohort